text.section:
A general receiver may retain from moneys received and held pursuant to § 8.01-582, compensation for his services in such amount as the court deems reasonable, but not exceeding:

Ten dollars at receipt of the originating court order to receive funds, deposit funds, and establish files and accounting records with respect to those funds;


Ten dollars when all funds held for a beneficiary or beneficiaries are disbursed;


Ten dollars per draft or check for periodic and final disbursements;


Five percent of the interest income earned;


Ten dollars for remitting funds to the State Treasurer and up to ten dollars per draft for remitting those funds; and


Fifty dollars for conducting a hearing to ascertain the identity or location of trust fund beneficiaries pursuant to § 8.01-586 as the court directs and $50 per hour for an appearance in court.
